From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:34:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 23/30] Verify activation issuance and exclude protected actor
 memory snapshots

MintSupervisorBootstrap now also checks the calling atelet's own Pod, and
the checks split into small helpers. atelet refuses a Run or Restore
whose activation names another worker, and refuses to checkpoint or
restore guest memory for a spec with a supervisor projection. Tests cover
the signed claims, each denial, the durable activation and its rotation,
the golden actor, and the restore boundary.

